      "writtenOn": "2025-04-26T00:51:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that would work since pointers can be reused. Really what you would want is `Ref\u003cdetail::WeakRefData\u003e` because that\u0027s still valid as long as there are any weakrefs. But there isn\u0027t a way to get that, and besides, it\u0027s weird.\n\nDo we really need to break this ref cycle? Seems like it\u0027s OK to break it manually like we did before, though I\u0027m unsure if something you did in this CL made it necessary.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "7dae0c85eed3bd7ac898d22eee8c8b723d394b88",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80878dc6_8cd2cbf3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/EventManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-30T01:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before, I was breaking the cycle by using just the `futureID`, but I realized that it doesn\u0027t work for `AllowSpontaneous` because the way that events are implemented in native is that they require a reference to them to not call their dtor which just completes the callback.\n\nRight now, the `EventManager` drops all events when the `Instance` is dropped, and the only reference to queue based events right now is in the `EventManager`. So somewhere else needs to hold a reference to the queue events, hence the weak reference to avoid the cycle.\n\nIf we wanted to avoid this, we would need to (1) update queues such that they have an external ref count, and (2) make the device hold an external queue reference until it\u0027s gone (because you can always get a new external queue reference from the device). I didn\u0027t want to add ways to hold external references in internal code, hence the use of weak refs instead.",
      "parentUuid": "e905e392_80f35e57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "7dae0c85eed3bd7ac898d22eee8c8b723d394b88",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "593f8ae0_41aa352d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/EventManager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-01T01:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Often we have a cycle we break it during shutdown (or whenever) to make sure it doesn\u0027t cause leaks. Is it possible to do that here? I\u0027m not exactly sure how or when we could do that though because I don\u0027t understand the lifetimes quite well enough.\n\nAnyway, the WeakRef is fine, but don\u0027t you still have the problem with mixed source wait validation?",
      "parentUuid": "80878dc6_8cd2cbf3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "7dae0c85eed3bd7ac898d22eee8c8b723d394b88",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
